      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 1489: 🔴 There is a race that can permanently block future reply-target loads for a conversation. If `swarmLoaded(id, ...)` arrives after `replyLoadsAnswered.remove(id)` is checked but before `replyLoadIds[id] \u003d key` executes, the callback stores `id` in `replyLoadsAnswered` and returns; then this code records `replyLoadIds[id]` too late, leaving `replyLoadsInFlight` never released for that conversation. Make publication/consumption of `id` atomic (e.g., store `replyLoadIds[id]` first, then consume `replyLoadsAnswered`, or protect both paths with a shared lock / `compute` sequence) so an early callback cannot be missed.",
